```java
@Service
class OrderService {
    private final ApplicationEventPublisher publisher; // the subject
    OrderService(ApplicationEventPublisher publisher) { this.publisher = publisher; }

    @Transactional
    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        order.setStatus(OrderStatus.CONFIRMED);
        // notify every observer without naming a single one of them
        publisher.publishEvent(new OrderPlacedEvent(order.getId()));
    }
}

record OrderPlacedEvent(Long orderId) {} // carries the data to observers

@Component
class EmailListener {                 // observer 1
    @EventListener                     // synchronous: runs in publisher's thread
    void onOrder(OrderPlacedEvent e) { System.out.println("Email for " + e.orderId()); }
}

@Component
class LoyaltyListener {               // observer 2
    @TransactionalEventListener(phase = TransactionPhase.AFTER_COMMIT)
    void onOrder(OrderPlacedEvent e) { System.out.println("Award points for " + e.orderId()); }
}
```

*Add a third listener tomorrow — `OrderService` never changes. That is Observer's decoupling.*

